<title>USA: U.S. Aug personal income rose 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug personal income rose 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Aug   Jul-Rev from  Jun-Rev from   May</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.6    0.1    0.1    0.9    0.9    0.5</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.5    0.1    0.1    0.8    0.8    1.4</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.5   -0.1   -0.1    0.7    0.8    1.3</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.6    0.2    0.2   -0.5   -0.4    0.8</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.5   Unch   Unch   -0.6   -0.4    0.7</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Aug  Jul-Rev from  Jun-Rev from    May</p>
<p> Income		   6,502  6,466  6,467  6,460  6,460  6,405</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,631  5,603  5,607  5,597  5,601  5,553</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,338  5,308  5,312  5,298  5,302  5,323</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,174  5,145  5,149  5,136  5,140  5,162</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   644    625    626    632    634    648</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,544  1,543  1,549  1,541  1,544  1,549</p>
<p> -Services		2,986  2,977  2,974  2,963  2,962  2,965</p>
<p> Personal Saving	  293    295    295    299    299    229</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.2    5.3    5.3    5.3    5.3    4.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Aug  Jul-Rev from  Jun-Rev from    May</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,667  3,637  3,638  3,643  3,643  3,597</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   683    676    678    675    676    672</p>
<p> -Services		1,273  1,260  1,260  1,263  1,263  1,239</p>
<p> -Government		645    643    642    640    640    639</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    520    520    523    519    520    516</p>
<p> -Farm			 45     47     50     48     49     46</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  474    473    473    471    471    470</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected August personal income to rise by 0.6 percent and spending to be up 0.5 percent.</p>
